{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And it shall come to pass afterward</b> — Rabbi Yeshuah said: This entire prophecy is for the future. And Rabbi Moshe the Kohen said: If so, why did he say אחרי כן and not והיה באחרית הימים? Perhaps this prophet lived in the days of Jehoshaphat; therefore he mentions the Valley of Jehoshaphat. And the prophets and the sons of the prophets were many, for many went out to speak with Elisha, and Obadiah alone hid a hundred [prophets] from them." "<b>Upon all flesh</b> — In the land of Israel, which is a fitting place for prophecy."], :book :joel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "ק' resolved as the abbreviation for מאה (a hundred), referring to Obadiah hiding a hundred prophets in 1 Kings 18:4."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Joel -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/yoel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:06:52.329910398Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}